# rofi retired — vicinae draws every menu now. Deleting a file from the source
# tree is not enough to make it leave a machine that already applied it:
# chezmoi only prunes orphans inside an `exact_` directory, and neither
# ~/.local/bin nor ~/.config is one. Without these lines the other machines
# would keep a full rofi config, 25 themes and eight dead scripts on PATH —
# including rofi-keybindings, which was renamed rather than removed and would
# sit next to hypr-keybindings looking like a live second copy.
# The rofi packages themselves are left alone: dropping them from hyprland.yaml
# stops them being installed, it does not uninstall them.
.config/rofi
.config/rofi/**
.local/share/rofi
.local/share/rofi/**
.local/bin/rofi-clipboard
.local/bin/rofi-dev
.local/bin/rofi-emoji
.local/bin/rofi-filesearch
.local/bin/rofi-keybindings
.local/bin/rofi-killwindow
.local/bin/rofi-quickactions
.local/bin/rofi-wts
# Menus that had no rofi- prefix but were rofi frontends all the same.
.local/bin/emoji-picker.sh
.local/bin/toggle-audio-switch.sh

# hyprpaper retired — awww is the wallpaper daemon, and has been since it landed
# in graphical-session.target.wants next to awww-init. hyprpaper's service was
# never enabled there, so its config and its slice drop-in were applied to every
# machine and read by nothing: the config still named colorful.jpg long after
# picking a wallpaper stopped going anywhere near it. Same pruning rule as rofi
# above — deleting the source is not enough outside an `exact_` directory.
# The hyprpaper package is left installed; dropping it from hyprland.yaml only
# stops the next machine getting it.
.config/hypr/hyprpaper.conf
.config/systemd/user/hyprpaper.service.d
.config/systemd/user/hyprpaper.service.d/**

# fish config retired — it was set up to try fish out, never used, and drifted
# as a second copy of every zsh rc.d file. Same pruning rule as rofi above:
# deleting the source tree does not clean a machine that already applied it.
# The `fish` package stays in base.yaml, and must: cachyos-fish-config,
# fisher, fish-autopair and fish-pure-prompt all require it, so dropping it
# from the yaml would not take it off any machine anyway.
# Listed file by file rather than as `.config/fish/**` on purpose — conf.d also
# holds uv's own uv.env.fish, and fish_variables is fish's state, not ours. Same
# reason functions/ and completions/ are not globbed either: those two are where
# `fisher` installs a plugin's halves, and a glob would delete them on every
# apply and leave the conf.d half behind. These are every fish file this repo
# ever shipped — `git log --diff-filter=D` over home/dot_config/fish/ is the
# list, and the five older entries above complete it.
.config/fish/config.fish
.config/fish/local.fish
.config/fish/conf.d/00-env.fish
.config/fish/conf.d/05-options.fish
.config/fish/conf.d/10-completions.fish
